# Stokit V2 — environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in your values. Never commit .env.

# ── AUTH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ── RECEIPT SCANNING (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE live receipt path. Camera and photo-library captures are sent as base64
# to this Supabase Edge Function, which holds the AI provider key server-side.
# The key never ships in the client bundle.
#
#   app/(tabs)/shopping.tsx  pickImage()
#     → core/services/aiReceipts.ts  extractReceiptItems()
#       → XHR POST to this URL (Supabase JWT in the Authorization header)
#
# This variable alone gates the feature: lib/config.ts `hasOpenAiKey()` is
# `Boolean(receiptScanUrl)` — despite the name it reads this URL, not a key.
# Unset it and the app shows "Receipt Scan Unavailable". Do not remove.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RECEIPT_SCAN_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/scan-receipt

# ── UNUSED / DEPRECATED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# DEPRECATED — no longer read by any code path. Client-side OCR lived in
# core/services/ocr.ts, which has had zero callers since receipt scanning moved
# to the Edge Function above. Safe to leave unset; setting it does nothing.
EXPO_PUBLIC_OCR_SPACE_KEY=your_ocr_space_key_here
#
# UNUSED — never read by any code. Store logos come from the token-free Google
# Favicon endpoint (core/services/storeBrands.ts `gf()`), so no token is needed.
EXPO_PUBLIC_LOGODEV_TOKEN=pk_your_token_here

# ── STORE DISCOVERY (premium upgrade) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Google Cloud API key — used ONLY for store discovery, in core/services/places.ts:
#   • Places API   — nearbysearch, textsearch, autocomplete, place details
#   • Geocoding API — ZIP/address lookup
# Create at: https://console.cloud.google.com
# Enable EXACTLY: Places API + Geocoding API
#
# Do NOT enable Cloud Vision on this key. Receipts are parsed server-side by the
# Edge Function above; the only Vision call site is the dead core/services/ocr.ts,
# and it sends no bundle-identifier header, so it would fail under an iOS
# application restriction anyway.
#
# All five live Places/Geocoding calls send `X-Ios-Bundle-Identifier`, so an iOS
# app restriction for com.hewadadil.pantrypal is compatible with every one.
# NOTE: nearbysearch and textsearch return an empty list on failure — they do NOT
# fall back to Geoapify while this key is set. Verify store search immediately
# after changing any restriction.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza_your_google_key_here
#
# Geoapify key — the store-discovery fallback, also in core/services/places.ts.
# Live in production. Two distinct roles:
#   • While EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_API_KEY is set, this serves GEOCODING ONLY, as the
#     error fallback when the Google geocode call fails (nearby and text search
#     return an empty list instead of falling through — see the note above).
#   • With no Google key set, this becomes the primary provider for nearby
#     search, name search and geocoding, with OpenStreetMap as final fallback.
# Geoapify supports no iOS bundle restriction, so a request quota above realistic
# peak plus usage alerts is the practical control. Keep the quota high enough
# that the geocode fallback is never throttled at the moment Google fails.
# Create at: https://myprojects.geoapify.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=
